"""Current answering experiments, with concise status and real saved examples."""
import json
from html import escape as e
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def render(t):
 d=json.loads((ROOT/'research/answering-study/progress.json').read_text());body='<header class="hero"><h1>Experiment progress</h1></header><section class="section" id="summary"><ul class="brief"><li>Source-reviewed reference answers for all 105 recorded questions; '+str(d['source_reviewed_references'])+' source reviews are recorded so far.</li><li>Launched six matched questions with supporting speech or the original longer meeting history.</li><li>Moshi and MiniCPM finished their native audio runs; DuplexOmni is processing the longer histories.</li><li>Completed both Qwen3-30B text pilots and source-reviewed all 48 final answers.</li><li>Keep generation, independent speech transcription and source-based answer review as separate progress counts.</li></ul><p><a href="#answering-native">S1 pilot</a> · <a href="#answering-text">What to think</a> · <a href="#answering-inputs">Questions and input audio</a> · <a href="#answering-references">References</a> · <a href="#completed-microphone-study">Completed microphone study</a></p><p>Published snapshot: '+e(d['updated_utc'])+'. This page is a saved snapshot; local run records update during inference.</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="answering-native"><h2>Matched S1 answering pilot</h2><p>Six distinct questions cover task ownership, a dropped task, an unresolved design choice, presentation time, outreach responsibilities and P1’s folder status. Five development questions come from the existing development meetings; P1 remains a previously inspected diagnostic. Each model has twelve paired inputs plus one short DailyTalk runtime control. The supporting-audio condition is explicitly edited: only earlier source passages are retained, in order, followed by the unchanged question insertion. The other condition retains the original meeting prefix. Neither condition supplies reference answers or enrollment audio to S1.</p>'
 body+=t('Saved native outputs are separate from independent response ASR and source review; these are pilot counts, not full-bank accuracy.',['Model','Saved / 13','Speech ASR available','Source-reviewed','Job state'],[[e(n['model']),str(n['completed_outputs'])+'/13',str(n['transcribed_outputs']),str(n['reviewed_outputs']),e(n['state'])] for n in d['native_models']])
 body+='<p>Moshi uses its native prompt interface; MiniCPM and DuplexOmni receive a fixed meeting-role instruction without question-specific facts. Native packet sizes are 80 ms, 1 s and 480 ms respectively. Every packet receives its normal model step; generated state is retained. DuplexOmni uses constrained listening and the known question end to start answering; the other models retain their native speaking decisions. These controlled accuracy runs do not measure conversational latency.</p><p>Up to 60 seconds of silent input follows each request, preserving the shorter 19.2-second comparison through recorded packet decisions. Final-packet speech and native end-of-turn information are inspected before fixing the full-study endpoint. AMI speaker letters are transcript labels, not spoken participant names; speaker-identification limits are kept distinct from recalling a fact.</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="answering-text"><h2>What to think: first text comparison</h2><p>The text models receive ground-truth speaker-attributed transcripts. Earlier calls use only the past transcript, previous saved results and a fixed goal; they finish before the worker opens the user-request file. Chunk boundaries use the first observed meaningful sentence end at or after 25 seconds, with a 40-second cap, satisfying the 10–40 second plan; sparse chunks do not trigger a model call.</p>'
 body+=t('The three main conditions share the same reader, available history and decoding within each model; the selected-source control is an extra diagnostic.',['Condition','Earlier work','At the request'],[['Reactive','No earlier notes supplied','Full available transcript plus question.'],['Amortized summary','Short summaries with source IDs','Same transcript and question plus earlier summaries.'],['Amortized structured notes','Facts, owners, commitments, decision changes and open points','Same transcript and question plus earlier structured notes.'],['Selected-source diagnostic','No earlier work','Only curator-selected supporting speech in text plus the question; extra oracle selection, excluded from the main comparison.']])
 body+=t('There are 104 planned earlier-note calls and 24 request outputs per model; note validation here checks format/source IDs, not semantic correctness.',['Text model','Note calls / 104','Format/source-ID valid','Request outputs / 24','Request-time thinking tokens'],[[e(n['model']),str(n['note_calls'])+'/104',str(n['format_and_source_ID_valid_notes']),str(n['request_outputs'])+'/24',str(n['request_thinking_tokens']) if n['request_thinking_tokens'] is not None else 'N/A for Instruct' if n['model']=='instruct' else 'Pending'] for n in d['text_models']])
 body+='<p>Native Thinking tokens are counted separately from final output tokens. Instruct has no exposed thinking channel and is reported as N/A. All earlier computation, including unusable results, is retained for cost accounting. Accuracy and source review come before interpreting any token savings.</p>'
 if d.get('text_source_review_summaries'):
  labels={'reactive':'Reactive','amortized_summary':'Amortized summary','amortized_structured_notes':'Amortized structured notes'}
  body+=t('Codex source review of six development/diagnostic questions per condition; these are small pilot counts, not held-out benchmark accuracy.',['Reader','Condition','Complete answers / 6','Mean request thinking tokens','Mean ordinary output tokens'],[[e(r['model']),labels[r['condition']],str(r['complete'])+'/6',format(r['mean_request_thinking_tokens'],'.1f') if r['mean_request_thinking_tokens'] is not None else 'N/A',format(r['mean_request_ordinary_output_tokens'],'.1f')] for r in d['text_source_review_summaries'] if r['condition'] in labels])
  body+='<p><strong>Actual example:</strong> the outreach question asks who sends the main call and when. The source says A will send it today or tomorrow. Instruct answers “by the end of the week” in all three main conditions; saved notes do not fix that error. Thinking with structured notes gives the source-supported timing, but one six-question run cannot establish a general improvement.</p><p>Instruct generated '+format(d['text_models'][0]['amortized_generated_tokens'],',')+' tokens in earlier calls; Thinking generated '+format(d['text_models'][1]['amortized_generated_tokens'],',')+'. Invalid note outputs are not reused, but their computation is still counted. Format and source-ID checks do not certify the meaning of a note. <a href="research/answering-study/text-source-review.json">Per-answer source decisions</a> · <a href="research/answering-study/pilot-scoring-policy.json">Criteria saved before reviewing outputs</a></p>'
 body+='</section><section class="section" id="answering-inputs"><h2>Pilot questions and edited input previews</h2><p>These short previews contain the selected earlier speech and actual revised question; they are not full-prefix recordings or model responses. The original-history inputs remain available locally and all 105 questions remain in the planned final evaluation. Original speech is from the <a href="experiments/ami-question-audio.html">AMI corpus; source and license records</a>.</p>'
 for q in d['input_previews']:
  body+='<details><summary>'+e(q['meeting'])+' · '+e(q['question'])+'</summary><p>Supporting speech: '+format(q['support_seconds'],'.2f')+' seconds; original earlier history: '+format(q['original_history_seconds'],'.2f')+' seconds.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="'+e(q['audio'])+'" aria-label="'+e(q['question_id'])+' supporting speech and question"></audio></details>'
 body+='</section><section class="section" id="answering-references"><h2>Reference-answer validation</h2><p>All 105 reference answers have Codex source reviews, with required facts, optional details and earlier evidence. The 382 supporting passages match the available transcript and end before their question. The shared evaluator accepts all 105 reference records. This is source inspection with earlier checks reused where recorded; independent human ratings have not been collected.</p><p>The automatic reference generator and checker produced 105 proposals and checks. They remain auxiliary evidence: some citations used times instead of segment IDs, and the checker also rejected supported facts. A separate input audit found that the earnings-call text loader omitted untimed words; the corrected loader preserves them until their next timed anchor. The twelve affected references were rerun, and the six AMI pilot inputs are unchanged.</p><p><a href="research/answering-study/references-reviewed.json">Reviewed answers and source passages</a> · <a href="research/answering-study/reference-validation.json">Request, timing and evaluator checks</a> · <a href="research/answering-study/protocol.json">Frozen experiment design</a></p></section>'
 q=d.get('judge_qualification',{})
 body+='<section class="section" id="answering-judge"><h2>Scorer qualification</h2><p>The generic judge is tested on 68 earlier real answers to 17 questions from five meetings outside this audio pilot. Its prompt and thresholds were frozen before inference. It must complete every judgment, agree with the existing source-based pass/fail labels on at least 90%, falsely pass at most 5% of incomplete or wrong answers, and recover at least 85% of complete answers. These labels are earlier Codex reviews, not independent human ratings; the reader and judge also share a model family.</p><p>Current status: <strong>'+e(q.get('status','pending').replace('_',' '))+'</strong>. <a href="research/answering-study/judge-qualification.json">Recorded qualification results and disagreements</a>. The full-bank comparison remains gated on this check and caller review; a weak but correctly executed S1 baseline is a valid result.</p></section>'
 body+='<details id="answering-outputs"><summary>Actual saved responses and current transcription status</summary>'
 for n in d['native_models']:
  for c in n['cases']:
   if not c.get('audio'):continue
   body+='<details id="answering-'+e(n['model'])+'-'+e(c['id'])+'"><summary>'+e(n['model']+' · '+c['id']+' · '+c['status'].replace('_',' '))+'</summary><audio controls preload="none" src="'+e(c['audio'])+'" aria-label="'+e(n['model']+' '+c['id'])+' actual generated response"></audio><p><strong>Independent speech transcript:</strong> '+e(c.get('spoken_transcript') if c.get('spoken_transcript') is not None else 'Pending; ASR runs after this model shuts down.')+'</p><p><strong>Native response text:</strong> '+e(c.get('speech_text',c.get('generated_text','')) or '(empty)')+'</p><p><strong>Source review:</strong> '+('Recorded' if c.get('source_review') else 'Pending; speech generation alone is not an answer-accuracy result.')+'</p></details>'
 for n in d['text_models']:
  for a in n['answers']:
   review=a.get('source_review');reason=e(review['grade']+': '+review['reason']) if review else 'Pending'
   body+='<details><summary>'+e(n['model']+' · '+a['id'])+'</summary><p>'+e(a.get('answer') or 'No complete final answer extracted; inspect truncation and format flags.')+'</p><p>Request-time thinking tokens: '+(str(a['native_thinking_tokens']) if a['native_thinking_tokens'] is not None else 'N/A')+'; ordinary output tokens: '+str(a['ordinary_output_tokens'])+'. Source review: '+reason+'.</p></details>'
 body+='</details><details id="answering-resources"><summary>GPU allocation, sharing and dependencies</summary><p>Allocated now: '+str(d['active_GPUs'])+' GPUs; observed maximum: '+str(d['maximum_active_GPUs_observed'])+'; allowed maximum: four. Allocated cost so far: '+format(d['allocated_GPU_hours'],'.3f')+' GPU hours. Three native workers are independent; the reference worker and two text readers occupy one sequential lane. Within each native allocation, ASR starts only after all S1 components exit. Text readers share no live S1 or ASR service.</p>'
 body+=t('Per-job requested GPU type/VRAM and actual scheduler state; completed jobs no longer hold their GPUs.',['Stage / job','State','GPU count / type / VRAM','GPU role and dependency'],[[e(j['stage']+' / '+j['job']),e(j['state']),str(j['gpu_count'])+' / '+e(j['gpu_type_vram']),e(j['roles']['0']+'; '+j['dependencies'])] for j in d['jobs']])
 body+='<p><a href="research/answering-study/progress.json">Saved counts, outputs and allocation snapshot</a> · <a href="research/answering-study/audio-provenance.json">Lossless audio export checks</a> · <a href="research/answering-study/manifest.json">Bundle hashes</a> · <a href="todo.html">Project checklist</a> · <a href="daily-log.html">Daily log</a></p></details>'
 return body
